WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.506
After the LavishCars technical assessment, Ayman Lakhnati developed this independent, AI-assisted

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:13.059
marketplace concept. The objective is practical: help suppliers publish approved offers, help

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:19.611
customers discover suitable vehicles, and turn interest into structured inquiries. This walkthrough

00:00:19.611 --> 00:00:26.164
combines verified prototype screens with fresh API demonstrations. All suppliers, vehicles and

00:00:26.164 --> 00:00:33.808
prices are synthetic. It is a listings marketplace, with no payment or confirmed reservation.

00:00:35.008 --> 00:00:43.292
The showcase begins with a simple request: a luxury SUV in Dubai, for four days, below one thousand

00:00:43.292 --> 00:00:48.815
dirhams per day. The concierge extracts supported constraints, queries approved inventory, and

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:56.639
returns up to three real database records with prices and explanations. It can ask for a missing

00:00:56.639 --> 00:01:01.702
destination while preserving earlier budget and passenger details. The database remains

00:01:01.702 --> 00:01:06.764
authoritative for price, supplier eligibility and visibility. The no-key interpretation is

00:01:06.764 --> 00:01:12.287
deterministic, so the demonstration works without a paid model. An optional external-provider

00:01:12.287 --> 00:01:17.810
adapter is implemented, but a real model call has not been verified.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:24.832
The preference service makes the ranking explicit. Destination, budget, passenger capacity and

00:01:24.832 --> 00:01:31.139
required features constrain the eligible offers. A preferred category adds twenty ranking points,

00:01:31.139 --> 00:01:38.902
and an editorial occasion match adds ten. Ties use daily price, then listing identity. These are

00:01:38.902 --> 00:01:44.725
transparent rules, not invented match percentages or machine-learning accuracy claims. The customer

00:01:44.725 --> 00:01:52.973
can inspect the same vehicle record and request a quote. An inquiry is saved with its responsible

00:01:52.973 --> 00:01:59.766
listing, supplier and location before any notification attempt. It remains an inquiry, never a

00:01:59.766 --> 00:02:00.736
booking guarantee.

00:02:01.936 --> 00:02:08.645
For suppliers, the listing assistant turns rough vehicle notes into suggested fields, a concise

00:02:08.645 --> 00:02:13.916
description and completeness warnings. It recognizes existing catalog references and explicitly

00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:20.145
supplied facts. Unknown specifications remain for review. Suggestions must be previewed and applied

00:02:20.145 --> 00:02:28.292
to an editable draft. Applying them does not save, submit or publish a vehicle. The supplier still

00:02:28.292 --> 00:02:35.000
checks the details, uploads permitted images, saves the offer and submits it for administrator

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.230
review. Supplier identity comes from authentication, and private listings and inquiries are scoped

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:42.668
to that supplier.

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:51.290
Administrator approval is a real boundary in the backend. A published offer also requires an

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:58.218
approved, active supplier, an enabled market and no administrative hide. The same eligibility rule

00:02:58.218 --> 00:03:03.661
protects public search, vehicle details, recommendations and new inquiries. Supplier suspension

00:03:03.661 --> 00:03:09.599
removes public visibility without deleting business records. Material listing edits require renewed

00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:16.526
review. Customer inquiries are stored as structured CRM records, with controlled status updates. A

00:03:16.526 --> 00:03:23.454
notification failure cannot erase the saved request because the inquiry and outbox event commit

00:03:23.454 --> 00:03:23.949
together.

00:03:25.149 --> 00:03:31.600
The insights service summarizes actual account data: listing states, inquiry states, category

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:38.590
interest and the most-viewed vehicle details. View metrics count detail API requests, including

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:44.504
repeats and automated demonstrations. They are descriptive measures, not unique-customer conversion

00:03:44.504 --> 00:03:50.955
or demand forecasts. Photo assistance checks resolution, brightness and edge detail, detects

00:03:50.955 --> 00:03:57.407
identical normalized uploads, and provides a documented cover-candidate score. These local image

00:03:57.407 --> 00:04:04.934
heuristics support supplier review. They do not verify that a photograph contains a vehicle,

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:08.160
establish ownership, or infer exact specifications.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:15.143
The architecture respects LavishCars' existing WordPress investment. WordPress remains the intended

00:04:15.143 --> 00:04:21.977
marketing, content and SEO layer. Fast API and PostgreSQL own suppliers, normalized memberships,

00:04:21.977 --> 00:04:29.862
service areas, offers, approvals and inquiries. Next J S demonstrates the storefront and portals. A

00:04:29.862 --> 00:04:36.696
local WordPress bridge has been tested for catalog rendering and supplier suspension visibility.

00:04:36.696 --> 00:04:42.479
Verification includes twenty-two backend tests, four main browser scenarios, seven extended

00:04:42.479 --> 00:04:49.839
interface checks and five proxy checks. The build and lint pass locally. Remote continuous

00:04:49.839 --> 00:04:57.724
integration has a startup failure, and public deployment is still blocked by the hosting account

00:04:57.724 --> 00:04:58.250
setup.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:05.721
The result is a reviewable demonstration of the complete supplier-to-inquiry workflow, with grounded

00:05:05.721 --> 00:05:12.476
assistance where it helps. The repository includes the architecture, requirement audit, tests and an

00:05:12.476 --> 00:05:18.747
explicit production roadmap. The next conversation is about scope, trade-offs and how this

00:05:18.747 --> 00:05:25.019
foundation should fit LavishCars' priorities. This is an unofficial concept developed with AI

00:05:25.019 --> 00:05:27.914
assistance. The voice narration is synthetic.
